    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d711">

                <pb facs="0965" n="953" xml:id="pg953"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.50/1–245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-15">January 15,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have studied your
                    letter of January 1 to the President relating to the Treasury’s plan for
                    comprehensive financial aid to the U.S.S.R. during her reconstruction period. In
                    this connection you will have received paraphrases of Ambassador Harriman’s two
                    telegrams regarding the recent Soviet request for a large post-war
                    reconstruction credit.</p>
                <p>We have been considering these matters and would be very pleased to sit down with
                    you and members of the Treasury staff to discuss your plan and the Soviet
                    request.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
